WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:03.920
<i>Two months have passed since we arrived.</i>

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>In order to be helpful mages,</i>

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.560
Good morning, Sayb!

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.480
Morning!

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.400
<i>we each run a store now.</i>

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.840
Lovely weather again today.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.110
<i>As the village handymage,</i>

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.110
Yeah. I'll make your tea.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.730
<i>Hort takes on a variety of job requests.</i>

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.730
Thanks again, Sayb.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.880
<i>Kudo is using the healing magic he excels at</i>

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.640
<i>to serve as an assistant at the clinic.</i>

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.820
Morning, Kudo.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.160
Morning!

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.370
<i>And I run a magic shop out of this house,</i>

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.120
'Sup.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.980
<i>where I supply magic to those who need it.</i>

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.110
Sayb!

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.260
<b>Saybil's Magic Shop</b>

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.700
I enthusiastically seek your 
magic supply services again!

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.770
Yes, yes, yes!

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.440
I'm being filled up!

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.410
I can't get enough

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.690
of this <i>sensation</i> lately.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.440
Ah. Sorry, Hort.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.660
Are you okay?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.300
Huh?

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.660
Ah, a nosebleed!

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.740
You're too thirsty for it, dumb-dumb.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.450
If you take too much, you'll die.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.540
But...

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.910
Damn it! It really does feel g—

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:10.850
Gross...

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.400
Well, see you later!

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.260
Later.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.110
<i>As the days pass by,</i>

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.980
<i>bit by bit, I feel more used to life here.</i>

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.070
Good morning, Sayb!

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.230
Thou lookest well this morning.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.260
Used to life here, thou sayest?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.740
Episode 6
   Knowledge of Ignorance

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:02.740
So,

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.990
without ever leaving the house...

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.400
How wouldst thou get used to the village?

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.080
I swear.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.880
To think thou wouldst utterly 
avoid initiating interaction!

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.380
Art thou awaiting an invitation to dance,

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.640
like some anxious noble girl at a ball?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.090
I'm confining myself to my shop,

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.520
as a commoner apprentice mage.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.900
So thou know thou art a shut-in.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.400
But in the event someone's magic is depleted,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.380
I need to be here.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.650
And I have cleaning to do.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.560
And everyone's laundry.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.170
Including Hort's?

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:46.740
Yes.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.760
Hort struggles a little with cleaning.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.130
While I was cleaning the other day,

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.900
I found underwear that 
had fallen under her bed.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.250
Let me ask thee.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.630
Did Hort ask that thou do her laundry?

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.130
No. I decided to do it.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:09.350
And then Hort started 
hiding her underwear?

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.270
I don't think she was <i>hiding</i> it...

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.770
'Tis obvious that she was hiding it!

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.920
Listen up! This must stop!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.780
I cannot find the words to 
deride thy dunderheadedness!

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.780
That a nubile maiden should have the 
sweaty underwear she worked all day in

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.040
washed by a boy her age? Preposterous!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.750
What art thou thinking when thou does this?

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.630
That I could do with some 
soap to remove the stains.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.630
P-Professor Los?

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:45.130
Didst thou just say <i>stains</i>?!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.680
Well... underwear absorbs sweat, so...

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.890
If you don't wash a pair thoroughly...

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.600
Stains soon appear—

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.560
Stop! Stop!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.510
If anyone were to hear thee,

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:01.080
the women of the village would brand 
thee as an enterprising young pervert!

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.330
Just for discussing laundry?

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.130
'Tis not just any laundry!

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.740
'Tis a maiden’s freshly-worn underwear!

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.100
I imagine not, but...

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.920
Thou didst not mention underwear 
stains or grime to Hort, didst thou?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.880
No. I said I cleaned them, that's all

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:24.900
O gods...

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.460
Wh-What?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.360
Listen here, Sayb!

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.640
Removed clothing has 
one's scent, one's sweat...

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.770
and various <i>other</i> things soaked in!
 They're an extension of you!

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.910
Just imagine!

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.020
What if underwear thou just tookest off

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.070
had a large hairy man
 slobbering over them?

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.920
Spine-chilling, is it not?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.030
Indeed.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.870
In other words,

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.790
to Hort, I'm a big, hairy dude.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.040
Erm...

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.690
That is somewhat off the mark.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.240
'Tis quite the opposite.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.210
Hort...

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.360
likes thee, doesn't she?

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.550
Well... I'm not really sure.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.930
She fancies thee!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.350
Take her to the forest at night and say,

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.180
"You're cute." See what happens!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:20.060
Thou shalt shoot up the ladder of adulthood!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.660
So I'll become an old man.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.940
No! No! No!

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.170
That's not what that means!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.320
I'm sorry.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.580
There's a lot I don't know.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.080
Listen well. People present 
themselves to others.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.500
When they especially like someone,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.210
they want that person to 
see only their good parts.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.650
But...

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.210
It just feels like it's my job.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.330
If I don't do it, I feel so uneasy.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:55.470
With no memories, he experienced 
all manner of oppression

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.990
as practically a slave.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.840
I see.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.770
There, there, there.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.620
Thou art a good boy, Sayb.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.120
Uh, ah...

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.270
Thank you, Professor.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.000
Nevertheless...

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.660
With things this way, thou hast
 no time for thy studies.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.630
But compared to practicing casting,

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.790
focusing on supporting Hort and Kudo 
contributes more to the village in the end.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.440
Sayb, I'm almost out of 
my favorite tea leaves.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.960
Please fetch some from the forest.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:43.400
Huh?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.650
But the store...

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.320
What?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:50.240
Thou canst make time for Hort and Kudo.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:54.530
But thou canst not make 
time for me, is that it?

00:07:55.360 --> 00:08:00.120
The reason I do house chores is that 
I have a job that keeps me home.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.290
Wrong. Because thou 
never leavest thy home,

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.570
thou art finding tasks to do there.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.920
Wow. You're outside, Sayb!

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.530
This never happens.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.550
Oh... You're Uls's kid..

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.190
Come on!

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.680
Lai-os!

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.160
What're those leaves?

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.910
Oh, well...

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:24.270
Jump!

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.700
Jump!

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:27.400
Waiting in a particular house for customers,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.820
and waiting in a particular 
village for them...

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.260
Over here!

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.570
They're both the same thing.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.570
Laios!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.140
H-Hold on a moment.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.820
Aw, why?

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.580
Those leaves are this way.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.460
I'm too big to go this way.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.210
But my daddy has no problem 
coming this far with me.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.610
Oh... He comes with you?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:52.840
Uls does?

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.840
Um... Well, sometimes he does.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.600
Going any further would require tools.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.540
We should go back for now.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.980
Y-You think I'm lying, don't you!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:09.480
Fine! I'll go pick some, so why 
don't you just stand there.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.240
Laios, wait!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.520
Laios!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.100
Laios.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.310
Are you mad?

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.540
I'm not mad.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.830
But I lied.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.000
And now I don't know the way back.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.790
It's my fault for being tricked.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:39.670
So I think I'll probably 
be the one Uls scolds.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:40.760
What?!

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.270
B-But that's not fair!

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.020
I'll have my daddy get mad at <i>me</i>.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.260
'Cause you were nice...

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.990
You trusted me.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.230
A mouse?

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.750
Oh, Lilly!

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.350
Lilly?

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.960
Lilly, at the church.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.220
Lilly is friends with mice.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.910
Sayb, follow that mouse!

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:19.080
It'll show us an easy path to the village.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.770
It's the church.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.610
It's my mom!

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:54.840
<i>Lai</i>-<i>os</i>!

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.590
Good grief! It's always something.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.490
Mommy, I'm sorry!

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.640
I imagine you're tired from 
your stroll in the forest.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.820
Why don't you come inside and rest?

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.770
I'll provide you a meal.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.510
Oh, uh... okay.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.650
This is my first time 
going inside the church.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.580
Not just the church.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:23.170
In this small village, there are fewer 
places you <i>have</i> been than haven't.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.630
Lilly, why are you wearing that?

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:29.910
So I don't startle him.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:31.980
Just let him be startled.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.800
Now take that off.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:34.540
No.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:35.860
Lilly.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:38.300
No!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.430
<i>No</i>!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.930
A m-mouse!

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:51.060
No! No! Give it back!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:51.990
Lilly...

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:53.940
Prepare a meal for our guest.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.410
What?

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.440
B-But...

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:01.700
He eats meals at Mercenary's bar.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.270
But still... I'm a rodent.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.200
Does that bother you?

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.570
Does what bother me?

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:11.020
You don't understand my question?

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.260
N-No, sorry.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:16.380
If you don't understand, then all the better.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:19.470
You cook, Ms. Lilly?

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.100
What is it?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:22.880
Nothing.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.890
Do you not cook, Father?

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:26.880
D-Don't!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.670
The Father's cooking is unbelievably bad.

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:30.390
It's scary!

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.890
So bad as to cause fear?

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:36.520
It's because I want our guest
 to have a proper meal

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.940
that I am asking <i>you</i>.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.920
Go ahead.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:44.810
Hot soup, bread, and honey.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.550
Honey?

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.120
We keep some bee hives in the forest.

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:54.990
And you were about to enter the 
bees' territory with Laios.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.100
The forest is a dangerous place.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.050
At night, there are even wolves.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:05.430
That's why adults harshly scold 
children who try to enter the forest.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:08.730
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.770
Not knowing is not a sin.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.850
But if you are going to 
enter an unknown location,

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:19.770
you ought to learn about 
whatever dangers you can.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:23.070
It's a matter of life and death.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.820
Do you want to die?

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.290
Hey, um,

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.420
the father is super ill-tempered.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.210
So no need to be down on yourself.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.320
O-Okay.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.260
This is delicious.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.090
And so why did you enter the forest?

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.540
Professor Los asked me to 
fetch some of these for her.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.000
This fragrance... Tea leaves, yes?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.850
You didn't even find 
out where they grow first?

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.380
If you had asked one of the 
adults in the village,

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.290
you would have found them easily.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.450
Since they grow next to Zero's house.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.530
Ignorance is not a sin,

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:16.690
but realize that being content 
with ignorance is harmful.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.510
It might motivate you to learn.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:21.960
Or do you

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.740
intend to spend your whole 
life shut inside that shop?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:30.510
Learning nothing, until one day 
Zero tells you you've passed?

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.470
Sayb!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.880
Wh-What's going on?

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.980
You almost never leave the shop.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.000
It's a long story.

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.080
I was treated to lunch...

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.690
Was it Lilly's cooking? 
Her food is delicious.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:49.700
Still, no matter how good the food,

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:51.670
this is a bad look.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.440
Did you get hurt?

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.780
There's blood on your sleeve.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:05.090
No, not me... Mercenary.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:10.470
Lately the forest creatures have been 
trampling the neighboring village's fields.

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:15.140
So I headed out with Mercenary.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.580
But on the way, we were 
attacked by a pack of wolves.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.610
I panicked and tried to cast...

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.860
But the incantation took too long.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.270
Mercenary protected me, but...

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.620
I... hit him with my spell.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.810
I came to get Lilly.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:46.260
Mercenary wants her... to handle the bar...

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:47.880
Hort.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.620
Hey, hey. Um...

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.420
He got hit on purpose.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.140
Because he'd still be fine.

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:59.770
But he was incredibly mad.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.650
He yelled at me not to start 
incantations I can't finish.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:07.450
Maybe I shouldn't become a mage!

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:11.540
It's okay. It's okay.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.750
My goodness.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.460
I didn't expect for thee to run into Hort.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.090
Professor Los?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.760
Thou hast a job, Sayb!

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.270
As a magic supplier!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.790
Mud-Black Witch!

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.180
I have brought the magic supplier!

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.440
Thank you, Dawn Witch.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.830
Apologies, young man.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:46.770
I'll borrow a bit.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:24.520
Was the kiss really necessary?

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:29.980
Getting jealous of the 
kid who saved your life?

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.250
That's shameful, Mercenary.

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:35.900
Um...

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.430
Is Hort going to be expelled?

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.240
What?

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.990
Is she?

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.500
I see no reason for it.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:49.130
But Hort said Mercenary was incredibly mad...

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.130
You're darn right I was!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.750
It's a matter of life and death.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.960
I ain't so nice that I'd 
bother lecturin' somebody

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:58.640
I had no intention of teaming up with again.

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:01.260
I scolded her because 
there'll be a next time.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.450
A next time...

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:07.560
It's my fault for being tricked.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:10.860
I'll have my daddy get mad at <i>me</i>.

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:14.610
I see. There'll be a next time...

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.900
I have to go see Laios.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.140
Oh.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:20.680
Um,

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.200
Professor Zero...

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.290
Please share some of these tea 
leaves with Professor Los.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:27.980
Bye.

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:35.410
It's more rational for him 
to support the other two?

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.520
The young man said that?

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:37.940
Indeed.

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:40.760
So he's expending his energy 
on cleaning and laundry,

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.950
and staying shut inside the house.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:48.020
And so I asked him to gather tea leaves.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:51.620
I wanted to give him a reason to come here.

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:57.280
In a small amount of time, he's fallen 
quite far behind the other two.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:01.000
Just because the other two are hurrying,

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.990
doesn't mean the young man must 
run at the same speed, too.

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:08.180
It seems fine to me.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.790
Why make him study if he doesn't want to?

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:14.570
He's contributing plenty 
just being a magic supplier.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.750
That is true.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.000
No, no, no!

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.560
I wanna see my ducklings to 
become crazy amazing mages,

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:29.630
and watch them turn the world upside-down!

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:30.990
What do we do?

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.060
What if Sayb continues not to learn magic,

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.440
and announces that he'll make 
his living as a magic supplier?

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:38.740
I'd just let him do what he wants.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.450
I need to get back to the bar. I'm leaving.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.640
Can I really leave this to you?

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:50.830
What, do you think I'm so incompetent 
I can't even inspect the village?

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.640
Quit joking around.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:56.140
You surely have some feelings
when it comes to Saybil.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:02.720
So you think I'd tie up a kid 
who's never even met his father,

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.210
and try him for his father's crimes?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.070
I do, a little.

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:15.480
Mud-Black Witch, why is Mercenary's 
change of clothes here?

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.490
He frequently stays over.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:22.860
My goodness. How far have you two gotten?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:26.300
Is that truly what you wish to ask?

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.750
Indeed.

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.870
About the magic transfer earlier.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.350
I know.

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:39.060
After saying I wouldn't turn a family 
member into a tool for obtaining magic...

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.290
That wasn't my point.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:43.880
Though I said some harsh 
things the other day,

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:49.770
if Sayb is operating a magic shop, then taking
 the magic he provides is not a crime.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:54.140
And yet thou tookest only 
the slightest bit of magic.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:55.270
Why?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:01.780
If I as supervisor told him to give me all 
the magic I want, it would be exploitation.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.820
There is no guarantee his 
well of magic won't run dry.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:10.130
But as things stand,

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.500
thou wilt age and rot away.

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:17.930
That is normal, Dawn Witch.

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.850
I shall embrace it.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.510
I won't fear it.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.800
Besides,

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:28.230
I'll age and rot away with the one I love.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.550
Compared to the alternative,

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:31.580
it's far better.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.650
Why aren't you fighting?

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.740
You're Grandma's servant!

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:53.880
If <i>you</i> won't fight, then <i>I</i> will!

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.480
My lady, you can't!

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:01.800
I'll defeat Thirteen and avenge Grandma!

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:05.800
Now would be a good time to tell me.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:11.310
So, what is it ya want me to do?

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.330
Okay...

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:23.290
Laios, let's go play in the forest tomorrow.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:10.040
Next Episode  ""I Can't Save Anything""

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.290
Edgelizord!

00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:03.580
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:06.430
Next episode: "I Can't Save Anything."

00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:08.800
Hang in there, my ducklings!
